lanation\": \"氟西汀 alters the pharmacokinetics of co-administered medications by influencing metabolic pathways. Specifically, it increases 普罗帕酮血药浓度 (plasma propafenone concentration), as evidenced by statistically significant elevations in AUC and C_max for both d- and l-propafenone enantiomers, along with prolonged time to peak concentration. This necessitates enhanced therapeutic drug monitoring when co-prescribed. Additionally, fluoxetine inhibits CYP2D6 activity—though not other CYP450 enzymes—leading to elevated levels of tricyclic antidepressants and antipsychotics like clozapine, potentially triggering toxicity [Data: Relationships (2535, 2529)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Neonatal and reproductive risks are prominent among 氟西汀’s adverse effects\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Exposure to 氟西汀 during 妊娠后3个月 is linked to several neonatal complications, including 早产 (preterm birth), 新生儿适应性降低 (reduced neonatal adaptability), and 喂食时发绀 (cyanosis during feeding). These findings stem from a prospective study by Chambers et al. (1996), which demonstrated increased incidence of these outcomes in infants exposed to fluoxetine in late pregnancy. Furthermore, breastfeeding infants exposed via lactation may experience irritability, sleep disturbances, vomiting, or diarrhea, though most cases resolve upon discontinuation of nursing. These reproductive and developmental risks underscore the need for careful risk-benefit assessment in perinatal care [Data: Relationships (12818, 12817, 12791, 6581)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氟西汀 induces sexual dysfunction through serotonergic mechanisms\",\n            \"explanation\": \"A well-documented class effect of SSRIs, including 氟西汀, is sexual dysfunction. Specific adverse reactions include 不射精 (anejaculation), 射精延迟 (delayed ejaculation), 性乐高潮延迟 (delayed orgasm), 快感缺失 (anhedonia), and 女性乳房肥大 (female breast enlargement). While fluoxetine’s sexual side effect profile is milder than that of paroxetine or sertraline (with reported rates of 17% vs. 47% and 36%, respectively), these effects remain clinically significant. The mechanism involves 5-HT2A receptor agonism, which suppresses dopamine and norepinephrine release in cortical and hypothalamic regions, disrupting sexual arousal and response pathways [Data: Relationships (12776, 12800, 12809, 12808, 12797)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Extrapyramidal and neurological side effects occur, particularly in susceptible individuals\",\n            \"explanation\": \"氟西汀 can provoke extrapyramidal symptoms such as 四肢粗大震颤 (coarse limb tremors), 手臂僵直 (arm rigidity), and other movement disorders. These arise from fluoxetine’s action on 5-HT2A receptors in the nigrostriatal pathway, which inhibits dopamine release and mimics parkinsonian states. Case reports describe severe reactions—including confusion, hallucinations, diaphoresis, and tremor—following co-administration with amitriptyline, reversible upon drug discontinuation. Vulnerable groups include elderly patients, those with 脑损伤 or 亚临床性帕金森病, and individuals concurrently using antipsychotics, carbamazepine, or lithium [Data: Relationships (12792, 12814, 6576, 6585)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"Systemic and dermatological adverse reactions are documented\",\n            \"explanation\": \"Beyond neurological and reproductive effects, 氟西汀 is associated with systemic immune-mediated reactions. 淋巴结痛 (lymph node pain) occurs as part of a hypersensitivity syndrome that includes urticaria, fever, and arthralgia, typically emerging 2–3 weeks after treatment initiation and resolving within 0.5–2 weeks of discontinuation. The overall rate of such allergic reactions (~2%) is higher than with sertraline or paroxetine. Additionally, non-specific symptoms like 全身乏力 (generalized fatigue) are linked to fluoxetine’s inhibition of prefrontal NE and DA release via 5-HT2A activation, particularly noticeable during rest [Data: Relationships (12823, 12782)]\"\n        },\n        {\n            \"summary\": \"氟西汀 demonstrates complex neurochemical interactions affecting mood and anxiety\",\n            \"explanation\": \"While effective as an antidepressant, 氟西汀’s pharmacology contributes to paradoxical anxiety and insomnia in some patients. By blocking 5-HT2C receptors on GABAergic neurons in the hypothalamus, fluoxetine disinhibits norepinephrine neurons, leading to heightened arousal. This mechanism explains why fluoxetine has a higher incidence of anxiety and insomnia (10–15%) compared to other SSRIs, with ~5% of patients discontinuing treatment due to these effects. These neuropsychiatric side effects must be weighed against therapeutic benefits, especially in anxiety-prone individuals [Data: Relationships (6581, 12791)]\"\n        }\n    ],\n    \"rating\": 7.5,\n    \"rating_explanation\": \"The impact severity rating is high due to 氟西汀’s wide-ranging contraindications, significant drug interaction potential, and serious adverse effects affecting neonates, the nervous system, and cardiovascular function.\"\n}", "refusal": null, "role": "assistant", "annotations": null, "audio": null, "function_call": null, "tool_calls": null, "provider_specific_fields": {"refusal": null}}, "provider_specific_fields": {}}], "created": 1782126747, "model": "qwen3-max", "object": "chat.completion", "moderation": null, "service_tier": null, "system_fingerprint": null, "usage": {"completion_tokens": 1641, "prompt_tokens": 7458, "total_tokens": 9099, "completion_tokens_details": null, "prompt_tokens_details": {"audio_tokens": null, "cached_tokens": 1280}}, "formatted_response": null, "content": "{\n    \"title\": \"氟西汀 (Fluoxetine) Adverse Reaction and Contraindication Network\",\n    \"summary\": \"This community centers on the drug 氟西汀 (fluoxetine), a selective serotonin reuptake inhibitor (SSRI), and its extensive network of contraindications and adverse reactions. Fluoxetine is contraindicated